  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/DER/DerivativesContracts/Swaps/DispersionSwap">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/DER/DerivativesContracts/Swaps/StatisticalSwap"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nbeb74f669f624bb18a1a69dfd2fb1250"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">dispersion swap</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.sk3w.co/documents/volatility_trading.pdf"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">statistical derivative used to hedge on the magnitude of a price movement of an underlying asset</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>A variance swap is an instrument that allows investors to trade future realized (or historical) volatility against current implied volatility.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>Some strategies involve selling a variance swap on an index and buying the variance swaps on the individual constituents; this particular kind of spread trade is called a variance dispersion trade.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
    <cmns-av:synonym xml:lang="en">variance swap</cmns-av:synonym>
  </rdf:Description>
