  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FBC/ProductsAndServices/ClientsAndAccounts/AccountSpecificServiceAgreement">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/ProductsAndServices/ProductsAndServices/ServiceAgreement"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nc4dc2bbb1d424856ad7eed935625db5f"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N01732415dd634ba1936f8e314a24a88d"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N88fc0c701dfe4c62813f01f7e49354eb"/>
    <rdfs:label>account-specific service agreement</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>service-agreement that is account-specific, applicable in cases where a client might hold multiple accounts with differing terms and conditions</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>Customers of financial service providers frequently hold multiple accounts - brokerage accounts, checking and savings accounts, trust accounts, and so forth - which may have specific terms and conditions associated with them.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/LOAN/LoansSpecific/GreenLoans/SustainabilityAndBusinessStrategy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/GoalsAndObjectives/Objectives/BusinessStrategy"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Ne044a11409e8443c994b67e859e16b68"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nc1f4be7c940e47e68a4816dda3273f47"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N24a8f4a43f0848eeba6cb1aee42f4337"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">sustainability and business strategy</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">strategy for achieving specific business objectives related to sustainability (from an environmental and/or social and/or governance (ESG) perspective)</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:adaptedFrom xml:lang="en">https://www.lsta.org/content/sustainability-linked-loan-principles-sllp/</cmns-av:adaptedFrom>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote xml:lang="en">An SLL borrower should clearly communicate to its lender(s) its rationale for the selection of its KPI(s) (i.e. relevance, materiality, whether it is core to the borrower's overall business) and the motivation for the SPT(s) (i.e. ambition level, benchmarking approach and how the borrower intends to reach such SPTs). Borrowers are encouraged to position this information within the context of their overarching objectives, sustainability strategy, policy, sustainability commitments and/or processes relating to sustainability.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote xml:lang="en">SLLs aim to support a borrower's efforts in improving its sustainability profile over the term of the loan. They do so by aligning loan terms to the borrower's performance, which is measured using one or more sustainability KPIs that can be internal and/or external. The KPIs must be material to the borrower's core sustainability and business strategy, and address relevant ESG challenges of its industry sector.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
