  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/SEC/Debt/DebtInstruments/FullyIndexedInterestRate">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FBC/DebtAndEquities/Debt/FloatingInterestRate"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/QuantitiesAndUnits/Expression"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N3326b7c022174db69dc0f16c530af7f8"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N5857bf7ba5084f7da0e92a6f276081e2"/>
    <rdfs:label>fully-indexed interest rate</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>a variable interest rate that is calculated by adding a margin to a specified index rate</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>Fully indexed interest rates are used for variable rate credit products. The interest rate on a variable (adjustable) rate mortgage corresponds to a specific benchmark (often the prime rate, but sometimes LIBOR, the one-year constant-maturity Treasury, or other benchmarks) plus a spread (also called the margin. The margin on a fully indexed interest rate product is determined by the underwriter and based on the borrower's credit quality.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
