  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/LOAN/LoansSpecific/GreenLoans/EnvironmentalProject">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/GoalsAndObjectives/Objectives/Project"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N37ea27ec5c6749678741f8c27d1f57d8"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nff85455f093c474f89039561a03a5627"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N38a4db08a5af47e9aa37eb659eb649d7"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N05a1d8658875454fa709fb14ebedfba4"/>
    <rdfs:label>environmental project</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>specific initiative, activity, or investment aimed at improving environmental sustainability, reducing ecological harm, or addressing environmental challenges</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>Key characteristics of an environmental or sustainability project include achieving measurable positive environmental outcomes, and aligning with broader sustainability goals, such as those outlined in international frameworks (e.g., the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), Paris Agreement).</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>Such projects are designed to align with environmental goals, such as mitigating climate change, conserving natural resources, protecting biodiversity, and promoting a circular economy.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
