  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/SEC/Funds/Funds/FundContract">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Ndedb9007eb8048bcb7f027ef0a2fab6c"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/BE/LegalEntities/FormalBusinessOrganizations/OrganizationCoveringAgreement"/>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote xml:lang="en">From ISO FIBIM "Umbrella Fund" narrative: In securities, a collective investment scheme that has a contractual or a corporate form. When it has a contractual form, a fund is constituted under either the law of contract or under the trust law and thus it is not a legal entity. In its corporate form, a fund is a legal entity and is structured as a company.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">fund contract</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">contract that embodies and defines the fund legal form in cases where there is no independent organization</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/MD/DebtTemporal/DebtAnalytics/OptionAdjustedYield">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/MD/DebtTemporal/DebtAnalytics/DebtInstrumentYield"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">option adjusted yield</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NB specified as a spread. synonym: OAS Based on different Int Rate paths. There are different OAS models just like there are different Yield methods. Also would make reference to the Yield Curve - but these are parameters that go into that model. Limit this model at the point where it distinguishes the difference between things - we are not in a position to mathematically model the things themselves, just capture the basic facts.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
