    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">common metal that tarnishes, oxidizes, or corrodes relatively quickly when exposed to air or moisture, that is widely used in commercial and industrial applications, such as construction and manufacturing</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote xml:lang="en">Base metals or alloys include metals other than precious metals, such as copper, lead, zinc, tin, iron, steel, or brass. Note that iron and steel are included under metal and metal products in some classification schemes - see https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/WPU101 for example.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
