  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/SEC/Debt/SyntheticCDOs/SyntheticDebtInstrumentPoolFundingAsset">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N146326f3288e4237962a5bb24f0b2d87"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">synthetic debt instrument pool funding asset</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An asset which provides the funding for a synthetic debt instrument pool, as used in a synthetic CDO.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">From April 28 review session: CDS mechanization: Q: Are the CDS taken out on the constituents of the (non owned) pool or on some other instrument? A: There is funding to underpin the pool. The funding may be high grade debt or may be low grade. There is an undedrlying source of funds. then you swap (using CDS) into other risks. so I might lend to a government institution, and then sell protection against a whole series of corporates. So I've taken the high quality portfolio and added other risks to it. Or the other way round. conclusions:</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
