  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/MD/TemporalCore/SecurityCreditStatuses/InDefault">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/MD/TemporalCore/SecurityCreditStatuses/SecurityCreditStatus"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">in default</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The issuer has failed to pay somthing that they are contractually obliged to pay.</skos:definition>
    <skos:editorialNote xml:lang="en">(review 7 Oct 09) Does this exist as a term? This is a characteristic of the instrument not the rating. Because it's in default you can expect the rating to drop. Applies to instrument not to debtor. So a company may have 3 bond issues and may be defualt on only one. 14 Oct: Degrees of defaults e.g. tranche not paying interest due to losses on the underlying portrfolio; tranches being used to pay down more senior tranches.</skos:editorialNote>
  </rdf:Description>
