  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/Agreements/Contracts/UnilateralContract">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/Agreements/Contracts/WrittenContract"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N67e1a3a0e5ff4d459b2db6861cc0fe98"/>
    <rdfs:label>unilateral contract</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>contract in which one party makes an offer that can only be accepted through performance rather than a return promise</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>In a unilateral, or one-sided, contract, one party, known as the offeror, makes a promise in exchange for an act (or abstention from acting) by another party, known as the offeree. If the offeree acts on the offeror's promise, the offeror is legally obligated to fulfill the contract, but an offeree cannot be forced to act (or not act), because no return promise has been made to the offeror. After an offeree has performed, only one enforceable promise exists, that of the offeror.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FBC/DebtAndEquities/Debt/hasPrincipalRepaymentDate">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/DatesAndTimes/hasEndDate"/>
    <rdfs:label>has principal repayment date</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FBC/DebtAndEquities/Debt/PrincipalRepaymentTerms"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FBC/DebtAndEquities/Debt/"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/DatesAndTimes/Date"/>
    <skos:definition>relates an instrument to the date by which the principal must be repaid in full</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>Depending on the terms of the instrument (debt security, such as a bond, loan, etc.), this may be the date of a single payment of the debt principal or of the completion of scheduled partial redemption payments.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
