  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/LOAN/LoansSpecific/GreenLoans/EnvironmentalProgram">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/GoalsAndObjectives/Objectives/Program"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N023fa637209d410fa80eb27e4d9d5917"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Neadbbfcdc196439e9ed54d9d52c99de6"/>
    <rdfs:label>environmental program</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>broad scale initiative, activity, or investment aimed at improving environmental sustainability, reducing ecological harm, or addressing environmental challenges</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>Key characteristics of an environmental or sustainability program include achieving measurable positive environmental outcomes, and aligning with broader sustainability goals, such as those outlined in international frameworks (e.g., the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), Paris Agreement). Large scale environmental programs may consist of a number of projects aimed at addressing specific requirements that support the broader challenges outlined under the program.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
