  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/BE/FunctionalEntities/FunctionalEntities/Syndicate">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/Organizations/Organization"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Naee9f0853d0341238d27c82994588498"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">syndicate</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">temporary, self-organizing group of people, companies, corporations or entities organized as an alliance whose purpose is to transact some specific business, or to pursue or promote a shared interest</skos:definition>
    <skos:example xml:lang="en">For example, when a group of investment banks work together to bring a new issue of securities to the market, they form a distributing syndicate. Other types of syndicates are created for underwriting, banking, and insurance.</skos:example>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote xml:lang="en">A syndicate is a temporary alliance formed by people or businesses to handle a large transaction that would be hard to execute individually. Syndication makes it easy for businesses to pool their resources and share risks.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
