  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FBC/FinancialInstruments/FinancialInstruments/RedemptionProvision">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://spec.edmcouncil.org/fibo/ontology/FND/Agreements/Contracts/ContractualCommitment"/>
    <rdfs:label>redemption provision</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>contract provision enabling the issuer (writer) to regain possession through repayment of some stipulated price</skos:definition>
    <cmns-av:explanatoryNote>In general, redemption is synonymous with 'buy back' or 'cash in', depending on the kind of instrument. Redemption provisions are commonly applicable to the process of annulling a defeasible title, such as for a mortgage or tax sale, by paying the debt or fulfilling an obligation.</cmns-av:explanatoryNote>
  </rdf:Description>
